@startuml hl7-ballot-cycle
!theme plain
title HL7 Ballot and Publication Lifecycle for a FHIR IG

skinparam state {
  FontSize 11
  BorderColor #888888
}

[*] --> CIBuild

state CIBuild #FFECB3 : **CI Build — Draft**\nFMM 0–1 · Active development\nBreaking changes at any time

state DraftBallot #FFF9C4 : **Draft Ballot**\nFirst formal HL7 review\nFMM 1–2 · High change tolerance

state Connectathon #E8F5E9 : **Connectathon / Interop Test**\n≥ 3 independent systems\nResults reported to FMG (FMM 2)

state STUBallot #FFF9C4 : **STU Ballot**\nFMM 2 required\nCommunity ballot — negatives reconciled

state STU1 #DCEDC8 : **STU Release 1**\nFMM 3 · Official HL7 standard\nReady for production trial use

state STUn #C8E6C9 : **STU Release 2+**\nFMM 3–4 · Implementations accumulate\nAdditional ballot cycles as needed

state NormBallot #FFE0B2 : **Normative Ballot**\nFMM 5 required\nWG + FMG + TSC approval

state Normative #B2EBF2 : **Normative Publication**\nFMM 5 · Specification locked\nSafe for regulated infrastructure

CIBuild --> DraftBallot : project matures
DraftBallot --> Connectathon : feedback incorporated\n(FMM 1 reached)
Connectathon --> STUBallot : interop evidence\ndocumented (FMM 2)
STUBallot --> STU1 : ballot passed
STU1 --> STUn : further feedback\n+ implementations
STUn -right-> STUn : additional STU cycles\n(common for national IGs)
STUn --> NormBallot : FMM 5 evidence\n+ governance decision
NormBallot --> Normative : ballot passed

Normative --> [*]

@enduml
